  "aiContextParagraph": "The United States is currently experiencing its most significant measles outbreak in decades, leading to the loss of its measles-free status, a designation held for 26 years. Global health authorities and the CDC confirmed the shift in status following a surge in cases that began to break records in late 2026. Data shows the current infection numbers have eclipsed any period since 1991. The impact of the disease has been severe, with officials recording nine measles-related deaths across the country, including recent reports from Pennsylvania. Public health efforts to mitigate the spread are currently complicated by localized outbreaks in specific communities, prompting experts to emphasize the importance of community leaders and trusted messengers in encouraging vaccination efforts to curb the rising death toll and stop the transmission of the virus nationwide.",
